WEBVTT

﻿1

00:01:00.396 --> 00:01:01.251
You know,


00:01:02.171 --> 00:01:05.147
I do a shitload of reading
and studying and praying,


00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:07.382
and I've come to a few
conclusions I want to share.


00:01:08.312 --> 00:01:11.779
People look at politicians and celebrities
on the TV and the newspapers,


00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:13.977
glossy magazines.
What do they see?


00:01:14.887 --> 00:01:18.410
"I'm just like them.
" That's what they say. "I'm special.


00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:20.261
I'm different.
I could be any one of them."


00:01:20.281 --> 00:01:22.974
Well, guess what?
You can't. You know why?


00:01:23.331 --> 00:01:26.418
'Cause in reality, mediocrity's
where most people live.


00:01:26.503 --> 00:01:30.297
Mediocrity is the elephant in the room.
It's ubiquitous.


00:01:30.381 --> 00:01:33.213
Mediocrity in your schools.
It's in your dreams.


00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.781
It's in your family.


00:01:35.655 --> 00:01:37.262
And those of us who know this,


00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:41.642
those of us who understand the disease
of the dull, we do something about it.


00:01:41.662 --> 00:01:43.977
We do more because we have to.


00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:46.081
The deck was always
stacked against us.


00:01:46.325 --> 00:01:52.069
You're either a big leaguer, or you're a
slave clawing your way onto the "C" train.


00:01:52.089 --> 00:01:55.572
Some people say Jack Αbramoff moves
too fast, Jack Abramoff cuts corners.


00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:59.576
Well, I say to them, if that's the difference
between me and my family having a good life...


00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:02.759
and walkin' and using the subway
every day, then so be it.


00:02:03.172 --> 00:02:06.375
I will not allow my
family to be slaves.


00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:10.838
I will not allow the world
I touch to be vanilla.


00:02:10.922 --> 00:02:12.840
You say I'm selfish? Fuck you!


00:02:12.924 --> 00:02:14.842
I give back. I give back plenty.


00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:17.761
You say I... I got a big ego?
Fuck you twice!


00:02:17.846 --> 00:02:22.099
I'm humbly grateful for the wonderful
gifts that I've received here in America,


00:02:22.183 --> 00:02:24.893
the greatest country
on this planet.


00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:27.980
I'm Jack Abramoff.


00:02:28.064 --> 00:02:31.942
And oh, yeah,
I work out every day.


00:02:58.636 --> 00:03:02.431
Mr. Sprague.
Susan Schmidt of the Washington Post.


00:03:04.142 --> 00:03:06.476
Find it all right? Yeah.
Thanks for seeing me.


00:03:06.561 --> 00:03:08.729
I got a lot of questions for you.
Ah.


00:03:08.813 --> 00:03:10.731
Jack Abramoff, right?


00:03:10.815 --> 00:03:13.358
I hear he was charging your
tribe an exorbitant fee.


00:03:13.443 --> 00:03:15.861
Thirty million or more.


00:03:15.945 --> 00:03:18.113
So I guess you met his
partner, Mike Scanlon, too?


00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.657
Oh, yeah. He's a real cowboy.


00:03:20.742 --> 00:03:23.535
Looks like they might
be in some trouble.


00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:32.913
Jack?


00:03:33.064 --> 00:03:34.713
Honey. Jack. Dad!


00:03:34.797 --> 00:03:35.447
Mikey.


00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:37.716
Hey, I've been calling you all day, dude.
Where are you?


00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.968
I'm in L.A.
What the fuck are you doing in L.A.?


00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.595
Our world is collapsing here.


00:03:41.679 --> 00:03:43.759
Wait. What have you heard?
Are you gonna be indicted?


00:03:43.765 --> 00:03:46.934
Well, I got federal marshals looking for me, okay?
I've had a hundred media calls today.


00:03:47.018 --> 00:03:49.770
We're under horrific assault from
the worst forces in our culture.


00:03:49.854 --> 00:03:52.022
I know. I know. You're the only
one that's returned my calls.


00:03:52.106 --> 00:03:54.983
The president's probably destroying
every picture he ever took with you.


00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.736
Well, you're no one in this
town until you haven't met us.


00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:59.446
That isn't funny, Jack.


00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.823
Don't fucking mess
with my chi, dude.


00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.243
I'm serious.
We are super-fucked here, okay?


00:04:04.327 --> 00:04:06.411
They're calling us the
new Watergate, Jack.


00:04:06.496 --> 00:04:10.332
We're about to be on the Nightly News.
You need to get back to D.C., now.


00:04:12.669 --> 00:04:14.836
Step up to the line.


00:04:16.297 --> 00:04:18.298
Dear Mr. President,


00:04:19.842 --> 00:04:22.552
I write you this petition
with hope and prayers.


00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:27.391
As a man of faith, I have come to
see God move in mysterious ways.


00:04:29.185 --> 00:04:31.478
After we're born, he gives
us the choice of two paths.


00:04:31.562 --> 00:04:33.563
Please don't smile.


00:04:33.648 --> 00:04:36.024
I'm not smiling.


00:04:37.235 --> 00:04:39.611
Accept the world
for the way it is,


00:04:39.696 --> 00:04:41.863
or see it for how we
might want it to be.


00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.991
Turn to your right.


00:04:45.201 --> 00:04:46.702
Your right.


00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:51.999
To me, the choice was obvious.


00:04:53.084 --> 00:04:55.627
How long are you gonna
be holding me here?


00:04:55.712 --> 00:04:57.713
You can get that information
from your lawyer.


00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:00.132
I do get my own cell, right?


00:05:00.216 --> 00:05:03.051
And I only eat kosher, okay?


00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.970
You do serve kosher, don't you?


00:05:06.556 --> 00:05:09.599
Mr. Abramoff, this is a
federal holding facility.


00:05:09.684 --> 00:05:11.643
It's not kosher.


00:05:39.964 --> 00:05:41.631
Jack Abramoff.


00:05:43.426 --> 00:05:44.760
Snake.


00:05:45.928 --> 00:05:47.888
What are you in for, Snake?


00:05:48.765 --> 00:05:50.265
Assault and battery,


00:05:51.059 --> 00:05:52.726
resisting arrest.


00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:54.978
Chickenshit beef like that.


00:05:55.063 --> 00:05:57.189
How about you?


00:05:57.273 --> 00:06:00.525
Oh, me? I'm...


00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:04.404
I work in D.C.
I'm a... I'm a lobbyist.


00:06:04.489 --> 00:06:07.657
Lobbyist. That against the law?


00:06:29.972 --> 00:06:32.474
Next to God, faith and country,


00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:34.518
nothing is more important
than influence.


00:06:34.602 --> 00:06:36.686
Political influence.


00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:42.067
Influence with the powerful
is like influence with God.


00:06:42.151 --> 00:06:46.905
Without it, there's only eternal hellfire,
damnation and congressional logjam.


00:06:46.989 --> 00:06:51.868
Here the influence we wield is more
important than the air you breathe.


00:06:51.953 --> 00:06:56.206
As a licensed lobbyist, I am legally allowed
to accept money from special interests...


00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:59.418
in order to influence
Congress on their behalf.


00:06:59.502 --> 00:07:03.422
I'm essentially a conduit to
motivating sleepy lawmakers...


00:07:03.506 --> 00:07:05.590
into getting bills passed
and legislation done.


00:07:05.675 --> 00:07:08.969
Well, our client is extremely anxious
to know what's in your bill.


00:07:09.053 --> 00:07:10.971
The reality is,
without lobbyists,


00:07:11.055 --> 00:07:13.306
the wheels of Washington would
come to a grinding halt.


00:07:13.391 --> 00:07:15.600
About how much are you looking
to raise with the event?


00:07:15.685 --> 00:07:17.602
Can you tell me that
in dollar terms?


00:07:17.687 --> 00:07:20.439
Why? Because the most powerful
members of Congress...


00:07:20.523 --> 00:07:24.568
rely on lobbyists like me for information
to guide them on how to vote.


00:07:24.652 --> 00:07:29.364
And how they vote sometimes requires
taking them on fact-finding missions.


00:07:30.491 --> 00:07:32.617
Like House majority
leader Tom DeLay,


00:07:32.702 --> 00:07:35.871
who we brought to the Northern Mariana
Islands in the South Pacific...


00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:38.373
a U.S. territory where
my textile clients...


00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:40.792
produce American-made
designer clothes...


00:07:40.877 --> 00:07:43.170
without having to
pay minimum wage.


00:07:43.254 --> 00:07:45.714
Well, these folks seem happy.
How are you?


00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:47.591
Hello. Thank you. Uh-huh.


00:07:47.675 --> 00:07:50.760
I think we should be able to
vote favorably on this, Jack.


00:07:50.845 --> 00:07:54.347
For example, your top-of-the-line
stonewashed jeans...


00:07:54.432 --> 00:07:56.725
can stay on sale for 19.95...


00:07:56.809 --> 00:08:00.270
simply because labor costs in the
Marianas remain low. Morning.


00:08:00.354 --> 00:08:02.272
Jack is pushing Mr.
DeLay hard...


00:08:02.356 --> 00:08:05.108
to make sure the minimum wage legislation
stays off Congress's schedule.


00:08:05.193 --> 00:08:07.110
Hey, you troglodytes,
will you make sure...


00:08:07.195 --> 00:08:09.112
that DeLay gets the latest
export numbers from Willie...


00:08:09.197 --> 00:08:10.989
in case the Senate tries
to kill this thing?


00:08:11.073 --> 00:08:12.949
Oui, mon capitaine.


00:08:13.034 --> 00:08:17.579
Lobbying is nothing more than
American-style democracy in action.


00:08:17.663 --> 00:08:20.207
And the more influence we have,


00:08:20.291 --> 00:08:22.250
the bigger the smiles
on our kids' faces.


00:08:22.335 --> 00:08:23.543
Oh, my God!


00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:28.590
Good morning, gentlemen.
Grover, what brings you to the locker room?


00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:30.592
Don't even bother trying to
pitch him on our new clients.


00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:33.428
He has issues with helping
our native people.


00:08:33.513 --> 00:08:35.514
Just with Native
Americans, Jack.


00:08:35.598 --> 00:08:37.807
What do they have to do with
Americans for Tax Reform?


00:08:37.892 --> 00:08:39.434
I need your help on
this one, Grover.


00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:41.937
I need the congressional friends
in your organization...


00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:45.065
to understand that there are certain
American Indian tribes that need help.


00:08:45.149 --> 00:08:47.359
Jack, the United
States, from day one,


00:08:47.443 --> 00:08:50.862
was founded on the basis that you
could be or do anything you want to.


00:08:50.947 --> 00:08:52.864
You're in charge of
your own future.


00:08:52.949 --> 00:08:56.284
There's no ceiling. There's no floor.
You want to be a bum, you can be a bum.


00:08:56.369 --> 00:08:59.287
You want to accomplish great
things, you can do that too.


00:08:59.372 --> 00:09:03.041
So, if some Native Americans choose
to live in third world conditions,


00:09:03.125 --> 00:09:05.627
why is that my problem, hmm?


00:09:05.711 --> 00:09:07.379
Are those pistachios?


00:09:07.463 --> 00:09:09.714
- Yeah.
- Genius.


00:09:09.799 --> 00:09:12.634
- He's here, Jack.
- Listen. This is perfect for you, Grover.


00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:14.719
It's philanthropic.
I mean, the money we're saving them...


00:09:14.804 --> 00:09:17.013
is essentially paying for their
health clinics and schools.


00:09:17.098 --> 00:09:18.807
Help them help themselves.


00:09:18.891 --> 00:09:21.476
Yeah. Come on. There's no one in
this town as persuasive as you are.


00:09:21.561 --> 00:09:24.396
- You're a Harvard man, dude.
- Yeah, yeah. The man with the crimson tongue.


00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:28.608
Grover, all we're trying to do is
help these people empower themselves.


00:09:28.693 --> 00:09:31.945
Jack, I've known
you for 25 years.


00:09:32.029 --> 00:09:33.989
Why do I think your
social gravitas...


00:09:34.073 --> 00:09:38.034
is more than just about
health clinics and schools?


00:09:52.883 --> 00:09:54.884
Veuve Clicquot, sir.


00:09:54.969 --> 00:09:57.137
Thank you. You're welcome.


00:09:59.015 --> 00:10:01.433
Iced tea. Thank you.


00:10:01.517 --> 00:10:04.519
Merlot with three ice cubes.
Thank you.


00:10:04.604 --> 00:10:08.148
Dude, seriously, I think I once got
a lap dance from her at Nexus Gold.


00:10:08.232 --> 00:10:10.150
I wouldn't know, Mikey.
I'm married.


00:10:10.234 --> 00:10:13.570
I thought I recognized her too.
See? I knew it.


00:10:13.654 --> 00:10:17.574
I think the good Lord would prefer I
have deaf ears on this one, boys.


00:10:17.658 --> 00:10:19.117
We all set? Check.


00:10:19.201 --> 00:10:21.494
Eighteen holes, St.
Andrews, five-star hotel.


00:10:21.579 --> 00:10:24.956
Hugh Fraser, British Open champ, on hand
to give a lesson. La-di-fucking-da.


00:10:25.041 --> 00:10:29.127
Restaurant tour of Edinburgh and a two-day
stopover at the Hyde Park Oriental in London.


00:10:29.211 --> 00:10:31.963
Oh. V.l.P.
tickets to The Lion King for Tom.


00:10:32.048 --> 00:10:33.798
Great.


00:10:38.929 --> 00:10:43.141
Okay.
Nice soft grip, soft hands.


00:10:43.225 --> 00:10:46.269
Take a whack at her. Go on.


00:10:46.354 --> 00:10:49.356
You made contact. Great.
Now I gotta sandbag my drive...


00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:52.400
so Poncho doesn't spew in his shoes with envy?
Poncho's been primed.


00:10:52.485 --> 00:10:54.861
I've arranged to have his picture
taken with Bush when we get back.


00:10:54.945 --> 00:10:58.823
Three years ago, his tribe is weaving
pine needles and selling key chains.


00:10:58.908 --> 00:11:02.160
Now all he wants to do is drive a
Hummer and buy condos in Hawaii.


00:11:02.244 --> 00:11:06.331
Can you tell me why these clowns get
to own casinos and make 20 mil a year?


00:11:06.415 --> 00:11:08.166
Well, I don't know.
Maybe 300 years of genocide.


00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:11.170
That not a good enough reason for you, champ?
Oh. Are you part Mohawk now?


00:11:11.253 --> 00:11:12.962
Yes, indeed.


00:11:13.047 --> 00:11:15.090
Kemosabe.
One of the lost tribes of Israel.


00:11:15.174 --> 00:11:17.133
Yeah, yeah.
You're practically an Indian, dude.


00:11:17.218 --> 00:11:18.718
Probably why they
like you so much.


00:11:18.803 --> 00:11:20.929
That's what I'm talking about.


00:11:21.013 --> 00:11:23.014
You know what blows my mind?


00:11:23.099 --> 00:11:26.768
All these Indians are so damn rich, and
they're still acting like Wal-Mart shoppers.


00:11:26.852 --> 00:11:29.521
He's a multimillionaire,
Jack, with a $10 watch.


00:11:29.605 --> 00:11:32.023
Just think. If you and I could
access some of that liquid,


00:11:32.108 --> 00:11:34.234
we would be running D.C. in no time.


00:11:34.318 --> 00:11:36.236
What are you suggesting?


00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:40.407
I'm suggesting that they pay us a
ridiculous amount of money, okay?


00:11:40.491 --> 00:11:43.743
And then you and I can split
the fee 50-50 under the table.


00:11:43.828 --> 00:11:46.371
It's a little tough
on the Chippewa.


00:11:46.455 --> 00:11:48.707
Not to mention, is it legal?


00:11:48.791 --> 00:11:51.543
What are they gonna do?
Cancel my membership at the ACLU? Come on.


00:11:51.627 --> 00:11:54.546
Well, you know, I got a
limit on what I can charge.


00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:56.798
That sucks for you, but
I'm freelance, Jack.


00:11:56.882 --> 00:11:59.175
I'm grassroots, baby.


00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:02.011
You're always complaining
about living hand to mouth.


00:12:02.096 --> 00:12:05.432
You know what?
You deserve better.


00:12:05.516 --> 00:12:07.517
Okay?
And Chief Shanks-a-Lot there...


00:12:07.601 --> 00:12:10.687
is our ticket out
of hourly fee hell.


00:12:10.771 --> 00:12:12.731
That's it, Chief.


00:12:12.815 --> 00:12:16.651
Okay. Put together a pitch for Tonto.
Let's see what he says.


00:12:16.736 --> 00:12:18.903
Looks good.


00:12:18.988 --> 00:12:21.865
Now, Chief, it's a simple thing.


00:12:21.949 --> 00:12:23.867
Look.
I've handled the Coushattas,


00:12:23.951 --> 00:12:26.411
the Tiguas, the Aguas Calientes,


00:12:26.495 --> 00:12:28.413
and I tell them all the
same thing, Chief:


00:12:28.497 --> 00:12:30.832
I know what it feels like to
be a persecuted minority.


00:12:30.916 --> 00:12:32.996
Yeah? Well, it's about time
you guys in Washington...


00:12:33.043 --> 00:12:35.253
finally did something
good for Indian people.


00:12:35.337 --> 00:12:37.756
Like give America back?


00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:40.675
You got a real sense of humor, Jack.
I like that.


00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:43.887
Look. The casino is a
plus if it's profitable.


00:12:43.971 --> 00:12:46.598
But in reality, the gaming
industry is very competitive.


00:12:46.682 --> 00:12:49.851
You know, the Jena tribe, they want
to open up their own casino now.


00:12:49.935 --> 00:12:51.770
They're just one state away.


00:12:51.854 --> 00:12:55.148
Yeah, and I know those guys.
They can be brutal.


00:12:56.776 --> 00:12:58.777
They can shut you
down mega-fast.


00:12:58.861 --> 00:13:01.404
No more Chippewa casino.


00:13:01.489 --> 00:13:03.490
You need our help, Chief.


00:13:03.574 --> 00:13:04.574
Hmm.


00:13:04.658 --> 00:13:06.493
You heard Mike's proposal?


00:13:06.577 --> 00:13:10.163
It's a tough call.
It's a hell of a fee you're asking for.


00:13:10.247 --> 00:13:14.125
Kind of a record, isn't it? But think
of the billions that you're gonna save.


00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:19.005
I can guarantee you that goddamn
Jena tribe casino will never open.


00:13:19.089 --> 00:13:22.425
And before you know it, the Jena tribe's
gonna be back selling moccasins.


00:13:23.844 --> 00:13:27.180
You know, Mr. Abramoff, we
can't afford to lose this one.


00:13:27.264 --> 00:13:29.933
You won't. Swear to God.


00:13:33.229 --> 00:13:36.022
Give me five!


00:13:36.106 --> 00:13:39.400
- A toast to Team Abramoff!
- Whoo!


00:13:39.485 --> 00:13:42.320
- To Team Abramoff.
- To giving America back to the Indians.


00:13:42.404 --> 00:13:44.405
All hail to Washington's
biggest retainers.


00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:46.741
Fuckin'-A!
You are no one in this town...


00:13:46.826 --> 00:13:49.202
unless you haven't met
Jack fuckin' Abramoff.


00:13:49.286 --> 00:13:50.787
Take it easy, Bill.


00:13:50.871 --> 00:13:53.152
- Jack, you know Emily, my fiancee. Everybody.
- Oh, sure.


00:13:53.165 --> 00:13:56.209
- From the, uh, Bush inaugural.
- I'll never forget that night.


00:13:56.293 --> 00:13:58.628
McCain was in his office
pounding Bushmills. "We lost!"


00:13:58.712 --> 00:14:02.090
It's nice to see the moderates
bleed from every orifice.


00:14:02.174 --> 00:14:04.217
Amen to that.


00:14:04.301 --> 00:14:07.428
Hey, Jack.
Those Polynesian factories you rep,


00:14:07.513 --> 00:14:09.639
uh, that make the blue jeans
on the Mariana Islands.


00:14:09.723 --> 00:14:11.349
Yeah? What about them?


00:14:11.433 --> 00:14:14.018
Word on the street is they're
goddamn sweatshops and rape camps.


00:14:14.103 --> 00:14:17.772
Oh, all you guys from the Washington
Post want to be Woodward and Bernstein.


00:14:17.857 --> 00:14:19.357
- Fuckin' pathetic.
- That so?


00:14:19.441 --> 00:14:22.110
The Labor Department just fined
your client nine million dollars.


00:14:22.194 --> 00:14:24.737
- Must be for something.
- Hey, listen, Ben Bradlee.


00:14:24.822 --> 00:14:27.323
Mistakes will happen, but the truth is
you can't tell me those immigrants...


00:14:27.408 --> 00:14:30.243
aren't making more money than they would in
China and sending it back to their families.


00:14:30.327 --> 00:14:33.246
That's right, Scotty. We're just greasing
the wheel with American dollars, baby.


00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:36.124
- Capitalism at its finest.
- Doing the Lord's work.


00:14:36.208 --> 00:14:38.835
Doesn't sound much like
American democracy to me.


00:14:38.919 --> 00:14:41.546
Don't be stupid.
No democracy, no fucking capitalism.


00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:43.756
No capitalism, no
fucking democracy.


00:14:43.841 --> 00:14:47.385
Only goddamn communistic
slave-driven bolshevism.


00:14:47.469 --> 00:14:50.054
- Thank you, Joe McCarthy.
- Fuckin' elitist!


00:14:50.139 --> 00:14:51.389
What?


00:14:51.473 --> 00:14:53.182
What is wrong with you? God.


00:14:53.267 --> 00:14:54.559
Calm down!


00:14:54.643 --> 00:14:57.395
Someone call 911.
Scott is a hemophiliac.


00:14:57.479 --> 00:15:00.106
You just hit a hemophiliac
reporter from the Washington Post!


00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:02.942
Come on! Oh, great.
Another bleeding heart liberal.


00:15:03.027 --> 00:15:06.321
It's okay. It's okay. Jesus.


00:15:07.156 --> 00:15:09.157
This isn't good.


00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.340
Enid, get DeLay for me, will ya?


00:15:25.424 --> 00:15:28.509
Should I remind him of Bible
class Thursday afternoon?


00:15:28.594 --> 00:15:30.595
- Bible class Thursday?
- Yeah.


00:15:30.679 --> 00:15:33.222
Jack, remember, I switched
it with your golf game.


00:15:34.308 --> 00:15:36.309
Well, Enid,


00:15:36.393 --> 00:15:40.271
you know, sometimes, even those of
us who occupy the Oval Office...


00:15:40.356 --> 00:15:42.523
can have our senior moments.


00:15:42.608 --> 00:15:44.734
Yes, Mr. President.


00:15:44.818 --> 00:15:48.571
Oh, Jack, Mr. Rouvelas is here.


00:15:48.656 --> 00:15:50.657
Make sure I see it before
it goes out, okay?


00:15:50.741 --> 00:15:52.992
- Manny.
- Let's grab a coffee.


00:15:53.077 --> 00:15:55.119
Hey, listen. If it's about the
Delail incident, no worries.


00:15:55.204 --> 00:15:57.288
I fired him yesterday.
The guy was a loose cannon.


00:15:57.373 --> 00:15:59.654
It's not like the Post is an
important paper in this town.


00:15:59.708 --> 00:16:01.709
Yeah.
Can we save this for later?


00:16:01.794 --> 00:16:04.337
Bear with me. It's important.


00:16:04.421 --> 00:16:07.715
All right, Manny.
So, where's the fire?


00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.759
We hired you because
the partners felt...


00:16:09.843 --> 00:16:12.512
we needed someone who had friends
in the Bush administration.


00:16:12.596 --> 00:16:14.514
It's not about friends, Manny.
It's about ideas.


00:16:14.598 --> 00:16:17.141
And you guys on the Right
used to have ideas.


00:16:17.226 --> 00:16:20.269
But now that communism is gone,
all you think about is money.


00:16:20.354 --> 00:16:22.480
So, did you invite me out
for an iced vanilla chai...


00:16:22.564 --> 00:16:24.524
just to remind me that I'm
a right-wing fascist?


00:16:24.608 --> 00:16:26.526
That's kind of beneath
you, isn't it, Manny?


00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:29.946
What's beneath me, Jack, are the
clients you drag into my shop.


00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:32.490
Those bottom-feeders in the rag
trade in the Mariana Islands.


00:16:32.574 --> 00:16:35.743
You know, there is an upside
for the poor Chinese.


00:16:35.828 --> 00:16:38.268
They get to send money back to
their families in the mainland.


00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:40.957
And look at all the great work we're
doing for the Choctaw, the Chippewa.


00:16:41.041 --> 00:16:43.251
That all sounds nice and
philanthropic, Jack,


00:16:43.335 --> 00:16:45.545
but you're buddies
with the White House.


00:16:45.629 --> 00:16:49.340
Hell, you're a good reason that idiot
cinched the Republican nomination.


00:16:49.425 --> 00:16:51.467
That's 'cause we destroyed
McCain in the South.


00:16:51.552 --> 00:16:53.302
Bush still owes you.


00:16:53.387 --> 00:16:57.765
Why not use that? Aim a little
higher when bringing in clients.


00:16:57.850 --> 00:16:59.767
Such as?


00:16:59.852 --> 00:17:03.521
Such as a Fortune
500 company or two.


00:17:03.605 --> 00:17:05.940
You mean rich, white people.


00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:11.237
Listen. I've got a situation
in Florida with a client...


00:17:11.321 --> 00:17:13.197
a very important client.


00:17:13.282 --> 00:17:16.659
Your background in gaming
might help us stickhandle it.


00:17:19.371 --> 00:17:23.124
So, Indians?


00:17:23.208 --> 00:17:25.001
No. Greeks.


00:17:25.085 --> 00:17:28.337
A guy in Florida
named Gus Boulis.


00:17:28.422 --> 00:17:31.090
Bankruptcy's just the
tip of his iceberg.


00:17:31.175 --> 00:17:32.759
He needs a buyer fast.


00:17:33.677 --> 00:17:35.470
It's a very lucrative casino op.


00:17:35.554 --> 00:17:37.847
Anybody who can afford
to get in will get rich.


00:17:40.893 --> 00:17:42.810
Anyway, Manny said you'd
have some clients...


00:17:42.895 --> 00:17:45.438
who might be interested
under the circumstances.


00:17:48.108 --> 00:17:50.109
Yeah. Okay, Art.
I'll look into it.


00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:42.620
Have you done your davening yet?
Mm-hmm.


00:18:42.704 --> 00:18:45.873
Then come to bed.
Kids are asleep. It's late.


00:18:48.043 --> 00:18:49.252
What?


00:18:49.336 --> 00:18:52.213
What are you thinking? About us.


00:18:53.382 --> 00:18:55.049
Seems like only yesterday...


00:18:55.134 --> 00:18:57.635
we were kicking around with
the College Republicans.


00:18:57.719 --> 00:19:02.056
Remember that time you brought
Pavarotti to Brandeis?


00:19:02.141 --> 00:19:04.058
Nobody thought you
could pull it off.


00:19:04.143 --> 00:19:06.227
All them lefties
listening to The Clash.


00:19:06.311 --> 00:19:08.312
Hey. I like Joe Strummer.


00:19:08.397 --> 00:19:10.482
Mmm. Maybe I should have
asked him to do a duet


00:19:10.483 --> 00:19:12.567
with Pavarotti. That would
have been something.


00:19:14.778 --> 00:19:17.738
I still love your
dorkiness, hon.


00:19:17.823 --> 00:19:20.616
Always thinking out of the box.


00:19:21.785 --> 00:19:23.703
Oh, Adrian...


00:19:23.787 --> 00:19:27.957
Nobody ever went the
distance with Creed.


00:19:28.041 --> 00:19:31.919
If they ring that bell
and I'm still standin',


00:19:32.004 --> 00:19:35.923
then I'll know I weren't just
another bum from the neighborhood.


00:19:40.512 --> 00:19:42.972
Come to bed.


00:19:44.516 --> 00:19:47.685
So this character Gus Boulis
comes down from Canada,


00:19:47.769 --> 00:19:50.688
opens up a chain of
sandwich shops in Miami.


00:19:50.772 --> 00:19:52.690
Then he cashes out,


00:19:52.774 --> 00:19:55.026
and he goes into the
cruise business,


00:19:55.110 --> 00:19:57.028
buys a fleet full of yachts.


00:19:57.112 --> 00:20:01.741
So, Boulis turns them into floating
casinos, runs out of nine ports.


00:20:01.825 --> 00:20:03.993
Tourists, retirees,
some high rollers.


00:20:04.077 --> 00:20:06.454
They call it "The
Cruise to Nowhere."


00:20:06.538 --> 00:20:09.582
But there's this Florida attorney general
who's got a hard-on for gamblers,


00:20:09.666 --> 00:20:11.918
looking for a technicality
to nail this guy.


00:20:12.002 --> 00:20:15.213
Problem is Boulis isn't a U.
S. citizen,


00:20:15.297 --> 00:20:19.926
which turns out to be a violation
of the Shipping Act of 1916.


00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:23.262
And then this idiot gets sloppy
about how he runs the casinos.


00:20:23.347 --> 00:20:25.640
He plays fast and
loose with the bets.


00:20:25.724 --> 00:20:27.600
He thinks he's still fooling
around with cold cuts.


00:20:27.684 --> 00:20:29.185
Blackjack. House wins.


00:20:29.269 --> 00:20:31.229
The customers start to complain.


00:20:31.313 --> 00:20:34.774
Pretty soon Boulis is catching heavy
grief with his gambling license.


00:20:34.858 --> 00:20:37.401
The gist of it is the feds
are forcing him to sell.


00:20:37.486 --> 00:20:39.904
He's got months to divest.
Gives me a window.


00:20:39.988 --> 00:20:42.198
Gives you a window?
What, are you serious?


00:20:42.282 --> 00:20:44.450
No. We're serious.


00:20:44.534 --> 00:20:47.745
145 million, dude?
How we gonna swing that?


00:20:47.829 --> 00:20:51.249
We're gonna use our most powerful
resource, Mikey: my imagination.


00:20:51.333 --> 00:20:53.960
Well, you better imagine us
as rich as the Chippewa then.


00:20:54.044 --> 00:20:57.463
So, what do you think of SunSail?
How do you think we should handle it?


00:20:57.547 --> 00:20:59.465
We need a front man.


00:20:59.549 --> 00:21:03.594
You know, someone strong enough to run a business,
but not so strong we can't control him.


00:21:03.679 --> 00:21:05.763
He needs to have his own money...


00:21:05.847 --> 00:21:08.724
so he can invest, keep
him loyal, honest.


00:21:09.977 --> 00:21:11.686
You know anybody like that?


00:21:17.109 --> 00:21:20.403
Kwikee-Mattress.
The last "S" is for "savings"!


00:21:22.864 --> 00:21:25.116
The lowest prices in
greater Bethesda,


00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:27.493
plus same-day delivery.


00:21:27.577 --> 00:21:31.289
The principles of the
Republican Party...


00:21:31.373 --> 00:21:35.376
more closely parallel the moral vision
of the God of Abraham than anyone else.


00:21:36.336 --> 00:21:39.630
So, the question: Does God...


00:21:39.715 --> 00:21:43.175
want people to be... liquid?


00:21:44.970 --> 00:21:48.097
And the answer is yes.
The answer is yes.


00:21:48.181 --> 00:21:52.143
Prosperity enables us
to do the right thing...


00:21:52.227 --> 00:21:54.687
to be able to help
our fellow man,


00:21:54.771 --> 00:21:58.024
to be stewards of civilization.


00:21:58.108 --> 00:22:00.526
Ln biblical times,


00:22:00.610 --> 00:22:03.362
taxes never rose above 20%,


00:22:03.447 --> 00:22:06.657
which is a lesson we
could learn today.


00:22:06.742 --> 00:22:10.828
Ladies and gentlemen, the Republican
Party lights the way for America...


00:22:10.912 --> 00:22:14.123
and, may I say, the
rest of the globe.


00:22:16.793 --> 00:22:18.169
Ralph.


00:22:18.253 --> 00:22:20.171
Really good stuff.
Thanks for coming.


00:22:20.255 --> 00:22:22.882
Inspirational, Jack.
Thanks, Congressman.


00:22:22.966 --> 00:22:23.758
Jack. Grover.


00:22:23.842 --> 00:22:25.176
We need to talk.


00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:26.302
Sure thing, Grover.


00:22:29.639 --> 00:22:33.100
"Stewards of civilization"?
Beautiful words, Jack.


00:22:33.185 --> 00:22:36.228
Well, I only take my cue from the
most powerful man in Congress.


00:22:36.313 --> 00:22:40.107
You remember Reverend Mueller from my
home district in Texas, don't you?


00:22:40.192 --> 00:22:42.109
Pleased to see you again, Mr.
Abramoff.


00:22:42.194 --> 00:22:44.554
You know, it's refreshing to see
both Jews and Christians...


00:22:44.571 --> 00:22:46.864
working together to make
this a better world.


00:22:46.948 --> 00:22:48.407
I'm inspired, Reverend.


00:22:48.492 --> 00:22:50.993
Karl. Nice to see you, Jack.


00:22:51.078 --> 00:22:53.329
The president asked me to
tell you to come by soon.


00:22:53.413 --> 00:22:56.123
Needs a little help with his golf swing.
Happy to. Thanks, Karl.


00:22:56.208 --> 00:22:57.625
Senator. Yeah.


00:22:57.709 --> 00:23:00.836
My, uh, clients have a, uh,
substantial check for your campaign.


00:23:00.921 --> 00:23:03.381
Really?
I can't thank you enough, Jack.


00:23:03.465 --> 00:23:06.258
You know, we're really
lucky to have you.


00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:10.846
Hey, hey, hey.
Slow down, you monkeys.


00:23:10.931 --> 00:23:13.808
Thank you. Be careful with that.
See you in the car.


00:23:13.892 --> 00:23:16.769
Watch your brother, okay, honey?
What did you think of my talk?


00:23:16.853 --> 00:23:21.482
Well, except for the part where God
wants us to be financially liquid.


00:23:21.566 --> 00:23:24.068
Sounded weird. Oh.


00:23:24.152 --> 00:23:27.113
I meant abundant.
It's... It means power.


00:23:27.197 --> 00:23:29.657
Remember Exodus 32,
the golden calf?


00:23:29.741 --> 00:23:31.659
The worship of the false idol?


00:23:31.743 --> 00:23:35.246
Hold the horses.
She's quoting scripture to me.


00:23:35.330 --> 00:23:39.500
Why, Pam Abramoff, when we met,
you were reading Cosmo magazine,


00:23:39.584 --> 00:23:42.586
mispronouncing all
them Yiddish words.


00:23:42.671 --> 00:23:44.588
Kvetch. Schlemiel.


00:23:44.673 --> 00:23:46.799
I think I'm getting
the hang of it.


00:23:46.883 --> 00:23:49.802
- Jack, nice speech.
- Hey, Adam. Thanks for showing up.


00:23:49.886 --> 00:23:53.848
Wow. Really gone for
the whole Jew package.


00:23:53.932 --> 00:23:57.726
Oh, I thought it made me look
more like, uh, Don Corleone.


00:23:57.811 --> 00:24:00.855
More like Fiddler on the Roof. Hey.
Don't knock Fiddler on the Roof.


00:24:00.939 --> 00:24:03.019
Lt was transformational for
me when I was a teenager.


00:24:03.066 --> 00:24:04.692
Made you want to be a milkman?


00:24:04.776 --> 00:24:06.902
No. Made me want
to be a real Jew.


00:24:06.987 --> 00:24:08.654
Hmm.


00:24:08.738 --> 00:24:11.282
Good-looking family you have.


00:24:11.366 --> 00:24:13.576
A big family you have.


00:24:13.660 --> 00:24:16.287
Pam, you remember Adam from
the College Republicans?


00:24:16.371 --> 00:24:17.746
Hello.


00:24:17.831 --> 00:24:19.874
Well, you've done an excellent
job raising the youngsters.


00:24:19.958 --> 00:24:22.626
I'm single again.
Swinging bachelor, I guess.


00:24:23.295 --> 00:24:24.879
Good luck with that.


00:24:24.963 --> 00:24:26.547
Listen. We need to talk.


00:24:26.631 --> 00:24:28.883
Can you swing by my house on Sunday?
We'll have dinner.


00:24:28.967 --> 00:24:31.343
You mean like a kind of date?


00:24:33.096 --> 00:24:36.265
What business could you possibly
have with a man like that?


00:24:36.349 --> 00:24:38.476
Honey, he's got a law degree
from Brooklyn College.


00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:40.644
He looks like a defendant
on Judge Judy.


00:24:40.729 --> 00:24:43.022
Honey.


00:24:43.899 --> 00:24:46.400
Have a little compassion.


00:24:46.485 --> 00:24:48.819
He's a partner in a
casino in Saint Martin.


00:24:48.904 --> 00:24:51.989
He's a respectable guy who knows a lot.
He could be a very useful partner.


00:24:52.073 --> 00:24:54.909
Useful for what?


00:24:54.993 --> 00:24:59.288
Ln five years, our family will
be completely legitimate.


00:24:59.372 --> 00:25:02.708
Would you please stop it with that, quoting
movies all the time. It's irritating.


00:25:02.792 --> 00:25:05.169
Oh, come on, honey.
You know I love the movies.


00:25:05.253 --> 00:25:07.171
And I am a Hollywood producer.


00:25:09.883 --> 00:25:13.177
You produced two Dolph
Lundgren movies, okay?


00:25:13.261 --> 00:25:15.513
You work in Washington now.


00:25:15.597 --> 00:25:18.724
Babe, Washington is
Hollywood with ugly faces.


00:25:18.808 --> 00:25:20.726
I'm serious, Jack.


00:25:20.810 --> 00:25:23.479
He makes me nervous.


00:25:23.563 --> 00:25:28.442
And another thing. I mean, how is that
we're late with the mortgage payment?


00:25:29.945 --> 00:25:31.987
We're okay, aren't we?


00:25:32.072 --> 00:25:35.199
Oh, yeah. No. This just must
be some accounting thing.


00:25:35.283 --> 00:25:37.284
I'll look into it
in the morning.


00:25:39.120 --> 00:25:41.664
Don't worry.
Put this on my desk.


00:25:44.292 --> 00:25:46.418
I'm watching you walk away.


00:25:47.837 --> 00:25:49.338
Still watching you walk away.


00:25:49.422 --> 00:25:51.298
Walk away some more.


00:26:00.267 --> 00:26:01.934
Everybody wins.


00:26:04.854 --> 00:26:09.733
As we all know, the gaming industry
has blown up across America.


00:26:09.818 --> 00:26:12.069
This phenomenon has
given great fortune,


00:26:12.153 --> 00:26:15.489
not only to our tribe... to
our people in general.


00:26:15.574 --> 00:26:18.117
But now we're at risk
of losing everything...


00:26:18.201 --> 00:26:20.452
to the competition of
our neighboring tribes.


00:26:20.537 --> 00:26:24.790
The point is we need help in
Washington, and we need help now.


00:26:24.874 --> 00:26:27.042
And as I said in my
written statement,


00:26:27.127 --> 00:26:29.211
Mr. Abramoff here has
my full support...


00:26:29.296 --> 00:26:33.841
in recommending that he have only the
best interests of our casinos at heart.


00:26:38.597 --> 00:26:42.933
Mr. Abramoff, I've, uh,
read your proposal.


00:26:43.018 --> 00:26:47.479
I see you want one million dollars
just as a retainer to start.


00:26:47.564 --> 00:26:51.442
Well, you're asking for the best, Mr. Sprague.
We are the best. We can get it done.


00:26:51.526 --> 00:26:54.069
You want to kick some ass
on the Hill, we can do it.


00:26:55.447 --> 00:26:57.156
Let's kick some ass.


00:27:00.660 --> 00:27:03.954
That was Dolph Lundgren, not
Schwarzenegger, in case you were confused.


00:27:04.039 --> 00:27:07.750
All right. Look. Here's my advice.
It's free today.


00:27:07.834 --> 00:27:11.086
You fellas hire Michael Scanlon and
Capitol Strategies and Ralph Reed here,


00:27:11.171 --> 00:27:12.963
who, as some of you may know,


00:27:13.048 --> 00:27:16.342
at one time was the very famous right
hand of the Reverend Pat Robertson.


00:27:16.426 --> 00:27:19.887
He can organize some high-wattage
Christian opposition...


00:27:19.971 --> 00:27:21.889
to this proposed casino
by the Jena tribe...


00:27:21.973 --> 00:27:25.476
and do to them what we did to
McCain in 2000... wipe 'em out.


00:27:25.560 --> 00:27:30.439
You want $30 million in
fees over three years.


00:27:30.523 --> 00:27:32.900
I could be president
myself for that.


00:27:37.072 --> 00:27:39.073
It's just too much money.


00:27:39.157 --> 00:27:42.242
The money's worth it.
Jack will lobby for us in Washington.


00:27:42.327 --> 00:27:45.537
He can help make us one of the most
powerful tribes in the region.


00:27:45.622 --> 00:27:47.706
Our people need
more health care.


00:27:47.791 --> 00:27:50.959
We need more education,
not influence.


00:27:51.044 --> 00:27:53.921
Mr. Sprague, you may not think you
need influence in Washington,


00:27:54.005 --> 00:27:57.424
but I'm telling you, to have direct
access to members of Congress...


00:27:57.509 --> 00:28:00.886
is gonna influence how
they vote on the very...


00:28:01.888 --> 00:28:03.555
Oh. Speak of the devil.


00:28:03.640 --> 00:28:05.808
It's the congressional
offices calling.


00:28:05.892 --> 00:28:07.810
It's, uh, House majority
leader Tom DeLay.


00:28:07.894 --> 00:28:10.104
Excuse me for a
moment, everyone.


00:28:10.188 --> 00:28:13.857
Tom, how's it going?
Jack, am I on time?


00:28:13.942 --> 00:28:17.361
Everything is terrific here.
In fact, I'm with the Chippewa now.


00:28:17.445 --> 00:28:19.905
Remind me not to order the
tuna from the cafeteria again.


00:28:19.989 --> 00:28:23.992
Yes. I will, uh, remind them of
what they're up against, sir.


00:28:25.537 --> 00:28:28.580
Yeah. And absolutely that they
can count on your full support.


00:28:28.665 --> 00:28:31.208
Great, Jack. I'll see you.


00:28:32.961 --> 00:28:36.338
Great, Tom. Say hi to the president for me.
I'll call you when I get back.


00:28:37.716 --> 00:28:39.925
I'm not bragging...


00:28:40.009 --> 00:28:42.636
when I tell you that we can have
effective and direct access...


00:28:42.721 --> 00:28:45.472
to members of Congress on behalf
of Screaming Eagle Resort.


00:28:46.975 --> 00:28:50.269
Otherwise, this beautiful
casino that you have here...


00:28:50.353 --> 00:28:52.938
is gonna shut down tight
and very quickly.


00:28:54.274 --> 00:28:56.191
Ln the current climate,


00:28:56.276 --> 00:28:58.736
we are barely breaking even now.


00:28:58.820 --> 00:29:01.155
I say the council votes no.


00:29:02.031 --> 00:29:03.782
Sorry, Mr. Abramoff.


00:29:06.870 --> 00:29:09.872
I'm going to have to agree.


00:29:09.956 --> 00:29:12.708
The council votes at 3:00 today, Mr.
Abramoff.


00:29:12.792 --> 00:29:14.752
But, uh,


00:29:14.836 --> 00:29:16.795
thanks for coming all this way.


00:29:21.760 --> 00:29:24.470
He's seriously messing with
the chi we had flowing.


00:29:24.554 --> 00:29:26.972
So Sprague is a subchief
on the council?


00:29:27.056 --> 00:29:30.350
It's an elected position.
Poncho has zero juice. Okay?


00:29:30.435 --> 00:29:32.478
What the hell is a
ceremonial chief anyway?


00:29:32.562 --> 00:29:35.272
Why didn't we know this before we wasted
a hundred grand taking him golfing?


00:29:35.356 --> 00:29:39.359
How the hell was I supposed to know
Poncho was the fucking queen of England?


00:29:42.197 --> 00:29:44.031
Well, Sprague's gotta go.


00:29:44.115 --> 00:29:46.283
When's the next
council election?


00:29:46.367 --> 00:29:48.827
You're not talking about messing
with the council election, are you?


00:29:48.912 --> 00:29:52.331
Because, you know, you're gonna be in
contravention of the Indian Act of 1968, mister.


00:29:52.415 --> 00:29:54.958
Well, let me tell you something. They're
fucking with our bread and butter, Mikey.


00:29:55.043 --> 00:29:58.670
I was gonna use that money as the down payment
on the SunSail opportunity with the Greek.


00:29:58.755 --> 00:30:01.882
Tell me about it. I just put a huge down
payment on this new house I'm buying.


00:30:01.966 --> 00:30:04.635
- What?
- The Du Pont mansion in Rehoboth Beach.


00:30:04.719 --> 00:30:06.428
I told you about it.
It's badass.


00:30:06.513 --> 00:30:09.473
And I've got a lease on a suite at the
Ritz-Carlton with this killer pool table.


00:30:09.557 --> 00:30:11.433
My overhead is insane right now.


00:30:11.518 --> 00:30:15.979
You haven't paid off your student loans. What
do you need with a mansion and a pool table?


00:30:16.064 --> 00:30:17.981
What? You're buying stuff.


00:30:18.066 --> 00:30:19.525
Worthwhile stuff.


00:30:19.609 --> 00:30:23.195
All right. Look. Just have Grover
keep Poncho entertained...


00:30:23.279 --> 00:30:26.907
and let him tell us mega-fast
when the next election is.


00:30:26.991 --> 00:30:30.577
Hey. I was in Florida 2000, dude.
Hanging chads, state troopers.


00:30:30.662 --> 00:30:32.913
This is gonna be a cakewalk.
All right?


00:30:32.997 --> 00:30:35.249
Tiptoe through the tulips.


00:30:37.126 --> 00:30:38.627
Hi there.


00:30:42.173 --> 00:30:43.924
Thank you.


00:30:48.471 --> 00:30:52.266
Be careful there, Mikey. She probably still
eats her Girl Scout cookies with milk.


00:31:00.275 --> 00:31:01.942
Thank you.


00:31:03.945 --> 00:31:05.863
Hey, baby doll.


00:31:05.947 --> 00:31:07.447
Hi. Whoo!


00:31:08.533 --> 00:31:10.450
Who the hell was that girl?


00:31:10.535 --> 00:31:12.661
You are so cute.


00:31:12.745 --> 00:31:16.039
She's an employee.
You gotta be nice to the help.


00:31:28.803 --> 00:31:31.430
For a Jew, I bet you get a
lot of cool Christmas cards.


00:31:31.514 --> 00:31:33.557
Oh, we see our share
of Nativity scenes.


00:31:33.641 --> 00:31:35.726
Hey. Look at you. Macho man.


00:31:35.810 --> 00:31:38.186
Oh, you didn't know I was a
guard at Beverly Hills High?


00:31:38.271 --> 00:31:41.189
Once knocked a kid ice-cold out from Inglewood.
Made the papers.


00:31:41.274 --> 00:31:44.860
I bet a lot of guys from Beverly
Hills went to the NFL, huh?


00:31:44.944 --> 00:31:47.988
Know what I majored in
in high school? Pool?


00:31:48.072 --> 00:31:50.115
No. Fuckin'.


00:31:50.199 --> 00:31:52.576
Really? How does it feel to
get a "C" in that class?


00:31:54.537 --> 00:31:58.457
All right. So you've gone from pool to selling mattresses?
That's quite an upgrade, Adam.


00:31:58.541 --> 00:32:00.834
I'm a very successful
mattress businessman.


00:32:00.919 --> 00:32:03.587
Really? 'Cause I hear
Kwikee-Mattress is in Chapter 11.


00:32:03.671 --> 00:32:07.966
Hey. I sold my franchise for
over seven figures and got out.


00:32:08.051 --> 00:32:11.428
Excellent. Because I've got a
new fantastic offer for you.


00:32:11.512 --> 00:32:13.221
Like what?


00:32:13.306 --> 00:32:15.432
SunSail Casinos.


00:32:16.434 --> 00:32:18.602
Offshore gambling?


00:32:18.686 --> 00:32:21.521
You know who you're dealing with?
Greenpeace?


00:32:24.943 --> 00:32:26.652
Trust me. I know.


00:32:26.736 --> 00:32:29.821
Adam, think of the fund-raising
possibilities, all right?


00:32:29.906 --> 00:32:32.866
It's like Vegas on crack.
The boats go out beyond the 12-mile limit.


00:32:32.951 --> 00:32:34.868
It's an all-cash business.


00:32:34.953 --> 00:32:37.329
Use your imagination, Adam.
'Cause I got plans.


00:32:37.413 --> 00:32:39.331
Yeah. Plans like Bugsy Malone.


00:32:39.415 --> 00:32:42.292
No. Plans like to open up my
own private Hebrew school.


00:32:42.377 --> 00:32:45.545
Public education sucks. You have no idea
what my kids have to deal with these days.


00:32:45.630 --> 00:32:47.673
Your own school? Yeah.


00:32:47.757 --> 00:32:49.800
Plus there's my foundation.
All the charity work I'm doing.


00:32:49.884 --> 00:32:53.220
Look. I'm trying to do important
stuff that matters for people.


00:32:54.555 --> 00:32:56.974
I...


00:32:57.058 --> 00:32:58.976
I...I don't know, Jack.


00:32:59.060 --> 00:33:01.979
I'm starting to see Charlie Manson as
my roommate for the next 10 years.


00:33:02.063 --> 00:33:05.440
This isn't a bunch of native people.
You're dealing with sharks here.


00:33:05.525 --> 00:33:07.901
I'm gonna say no.


00:33:07.986 --> 00:33:10.278
But thanks for the $65 steak.
It's delicious.


00:33:10.363 --> 00:33:13.657
Adam, just go down to Florida with my
business partner, Michael Scanlon,


00:33:13.741 --> 00:33:16.493
and you guys talk to
this Gus Boulis fellow.


00:33:16.577 --> 00:33:19.454
You're always asking me to give you something.
"Give me something. Give me something."


00:33:19.539 --> 00:33:21.289
Well, now I'm giving you
something, you schmuck.


00:33:21.374 --> 00:33:24.793
I was thinking something maybe a
little less hazardous to my person.


00:33:24.877 --> 00:33:27.504
I dealt with commies in Nicaragua,
generals in Pakistan.


00:33:27.588 --> 00:33:29.756
I've even dealt with
fucking Imelda Marcos.


00:33:29.841 --> 00:33:32.134
Why should I be afraid of a
Greek who makes sandwiches?


00:33:34.053 --> 00:33:35.762
What's Imelda like?


00:33:38.016 --> 00:33:40.225
She likes to play the piano
and sing show tunes.


00:33:40.309 --> 00:33:41.643
Really?


00:33:41.728 --> 00:33:44.229
Yeah. She's got a
pretty decent voice.


00:34:07.920 --> 00:34:11.423
Has all the subtlety
of a Thai whorehouse.


00:34:11.507 --> 00:34:14.067
Not that you would know what a
Thai whorehouse looks like, right?


00:34:15.803 --> 00:34:18.638
Looks like Boulis is
into family values.


00:34:18.723 --> 00:34:21.099
Looks like he hired
his whole family.


00:34:21.184 --> 00:34:24.478
Hey, guys.
I'm Chris, Gus's nephew.


00:34:24.562 --> 00:34:26.480
Gus is running a little late.


00:34:26.564 --> 00:34:29.066
You guys hungry?
You want something to drink?


00:34:29.150 --> 00:34:33.153
No, we're fine. I'll have a shot
of Cuervo and two Heinekens.


00:34:46.834 --> 00:34:50.295
I told Jack to forget about this place.
It's a fucking reptile cage.


00:34:50.379 --> 00:34:53.048
Boulis is doing mega
business here, dude.


00:34:56.344 --> 00:35:00.097
This blows. Whatever.
He's just trying to make a statement.


00:35:00.181 --> 00:35:02.849
This is how he operates?
We've been waiting an hour.


00:35:02.934 --> 00:35:05.727
I don't like it. I'm going back to Miami.
This is nuts. Whoa, whoa.


00:35:05.812 --> 00:35:07.938
Hang on. Adam, sit down.


00:35:08.022 --> 00:35:10.440
Sit down, okay?
Konstantinos Boulis.


00:35:10.525 --> 00:35:13.151
- Sorry to keep you.
- Hey. Mike Scanlon. Pleasure to meet you.


00:35:13.236 --> 00:35:14.736
Adam Kidan.


00:35:14.821 --> 00:35:18.657
Sorry Jack couldn't be here.
He sends his regards.


00:35:20.409 --> 00:35:23.009
You've done well for yourself, Gus.
Nice fleet of boats like this,


00:35:23.037 --> 00:35:24.704
dude, you gotta
be a content man.


00:35:24.789 --> 00:35:27.666
Yeah. Except for the
fuckin' attorney general.


00:35:27.750 --> 00:35:30.502
Because of him, I need to keep
what's left of my sanity.


00:35:32.171 --> 00:35:34.131
So, let's cut the crap.


00:35:35.049 --> 00:35:36.967
You and Jack plan
to pay my price?


00:35:37.051 --> 00:35:38.969
All right. Look.


00:35:39.053 --> 00:35:40.846
We can give you 20
cents on the dollar.


00:35:40.930 --> 00:35:43.306
That's the best we
can offer, dude.


00:35:43.391 --> 00:35:46.017
There's no negotiation.
You pay my price. That's it.


00:35:46.102 --> 00:35:50.063
Oh, yes. I keep a 10% interest.
I run the business.


00:35:51.107 --> 00:35:52.858
And don't call me "dude."


00:35:56.654 --> 00:35:59.197
You talkin' to me? Ah?


00:35:59.282 --> 00:36:01.074
Are you talkin' to me?


00:36:01.159 --> 00:36:03.410
Ah, it's your move. What the fu...


00:36:03.494 --> 00:36:05.996
You make the move. Huh?


00:36:06.080 --> 00:36:09.416
Sorry. Jack and his boys
watch too many movies.


00:36:09.500 --> 00:36:12.627
Movies? I didn't invite you
here to listen to comedians.


00:36:12.712 --> 00:36:14.921
- No, no. No. I was-
- What? You joke with me? Movies?


00:36:15.006 --> 00:36:16.464
Fairy tales? Get out!
Whoa, whoa.


00:36:16.549 --> 00:36:17.757
Fellas. Hey, hey.
You come back...


00:36:17.842 --> 00:36:19.551
when you can show my uncle
some respect, okay?


00:36:19.635 --> 00:36:21.344
No. I was just trying
to lighten the mood.


00:36:21.429 --> 00:36:23.180
Christos.


00:36:24.515 --> 00:36:27.350
Come on. Who doesn't
like impressions, right?


00:36:28.811 --> 00:36:30.896
What the fuck?


00:36:33.649 --> 00:36:36.193
Well, that went well.


00:36:36.277 --> 00:36:39.696
Fuckin' idiot.
Who doesn't negotiate?


00:36:39.780 --> 00:36:41.865
I know. I'm telling you.
He's a hard-ass, dude.


00:36:41.949 --> 00:36:45.702
You watch me put some hot sauce
in this fucker's tabbouleh.


00:36:45.786 --> 00:36:49.456
He's not gonna scare easy. I don't know how
the hell you're gonna get him to negotiate.


00:36:49.540 --> 00:36:52.250
Yeah. Well, you know what?
Try the Congress of the United States.


00:36:52.335 --> 00:36:54.377
Boulis will turn around, Mikey.
Trust me.


00:36:54.462 --> 00:36:56.880
- Hang on. Bob?
- Yeah, Jack.


00:36:56.964 --> 00:36:59.883
- Listen. I need a favor for a client.
- Sure. Name it.


00:36:59.967 --> 00:37:03.053
- Which tribe are we talking about?
- No. Not Indians. Greeks.


00:37:03.137 --> 00:37:05.138
Casino gambling
in South Florida.


00:37:05.223 --> 00:37:08.475
I represent the 18th
District of Ohio, Jack.


00:37:08.559 --> 00:37:11.394
It's a bit of a hot potato.
Can you deal me a pass on this one?


00:37:11.479 --> 00:37:15.065
After the money I've funneled to you this
year, Bob, no, I don't think you get a pass.


00:37:15.149 --> 00:37:18.610
All right? I need your help. I need it now.
Mike will send you the details.


00:37:18.694 --> 00:37:20.445
Thanks.


00:37:23.449 --> 00:37:24.991
So, here's the casino file.


00:37:25.076 --> 00:37:27.744
Jack expects to see you on
C-SPAN no later than Thursday.


00:37:27.828 --> 00:37:29.746
Tell him he's pushing it.


00:37:29.830 --> 00:37:32.123
Bob, he knows how busy you are
with the upcoming fall elections.


00:37:32.208 --> 00:37:33.959
Ln fact, if I'm not mistaken,


00:37:34.043 --> 00:37:37.003
he's organizing a huge fund-raiser
for you next Tuesday.


00:37:38.547 --> 00:37:40.507
Thank you, Mr. Speaker.


00:37:40.591 --> 00:37:43.385
I am an ardent supporter
of consumer rights.


00:37:43.469 --> 00:37:45.387
At the heart of my
comments today...


00:37:45.471 --> 00:37:48.139
is how certain gaming companies
treat their patrons.


00:37:48.224 --> 00:37:51.726
There are a few bad apples out there
who don't play by the rules...


00:37:51.811 --> 00:37:55.689
and who must be, uh,
weeded... weeded out.


00:37:55.773 --> 00:37:59.317
One such example is the
case of SunSail Casinos...


00:37:59.402 --> 00:38:01.111
and its proprietor, Gus Boulis.


00:38:01.195 --> 00:38:02.988
Yeah! Whoo! Yeah!


00:38:03.072 --> 00:38:05.073
You is the man. You is the man!


00:38:06.867 --> 00:38:08.576
What's all the
noise about, kids?


00:38:08.661 --> 00:38:12.080
Oh, hey, Manny. We're just working
hard finding a buyer for your client.


00:38:12.164 --> 00:38:14.332
Hey. Good. Glad to hear it.
Any live ones?


00:38:14.417 --> 00:38:16.334
Oh, yeah.
We're all over it, Manny.


00:38:16.419 --> 00:38:18.795
No shady ones from
the Marianas, okay?


00:38:18.879 --> 00:38:21.047
Absolutely.


00:38:22.091 --> 00:38:24.718
I serve this country
and no other.


00:38:31.726 --> 00:38:35.145
Listen. We need to get everything
we can on this Boulis, all right?


00:38:35.229 --> 00:38:37.272
I want you to call our
friends at Fox News...


00:38:37.356 --> 00:38:39.774
- and have DeLay hammer Jeb Bush down in Florida.
- Okay.


00:38:39.859 --> 00:38:41.860
No. Never mind.
I'll call DeLay myself.


00:38:41.944 --> 00:38:44.279
He wants me to hook him up with
the Harvard College Republicans.


00:38:44.363 --> 00:38:47.324
Thinks I can make him look good in
front of all those Ivy League monkeys.


00:38:47.408 --> 00:38:49.034
Yeah. Good luck with that.
You know what?


00:38:49.118 --> 00:38:51.328
He was a pest exterminator
in Laredo, Texas, dude.


00:38:51.412 --> 00:38:53.330
That's gonna be a huge
challenge in Cambridge.


00:38:53.414 --> 00:38:55.152
Hey, man. He clawed his way
up to majority leader.


00:38:55.153 --> 00:38:56.583
Now he's got his eyes
on the White House.


00:38:56.667 --> 00:38:59.294
DeLay? Are we talking
about the same guy here?


00:38:59.378 --> 00:39:03.465
He was an alcoholic with famous hot
tub parties before he met God.


00:39:07.178 --> 00:39:09.429
What the hell, dude?


00:39:09.513 --> 00:39:12.015
What the hell was that?


00:39:12.099 --> 00:39:15.018
Never before has an individual...


00:39:15.102 --> 00:39:17.062
who's been steadfast
to our principles...


00:39:17.146 --> 00:39:20.523
risen as high as House
majority leader Tom DeLay.


00:39:20.608 --> 00:39:22.567
Tom DeLay is the most effective...


00:39:22.651 --> 00:39:25.070
I would say he was the most
effective whip in the House,


00:39:25.154 --> 00:39:27.155
and I would say he's the most
effective majority leader,


00:39:27.239 --> 00:39:31.326
and thank God Tom DeLay is the majority
leader in the House of Representatives.


00:39:36.999 --> 00:39:39.542
And I would just like to
add one thing to that,


00:39:39.627 --> 00:39:42.879
because I'm sure we all want
to hear from Mr. DeLay.


00:39:42.963 --> 00:39:47.717
But Tom DeLay is who all of us
hope to be when we grow up.


00:39:47.802 --> 00:39:49.260
Tom.


00:39:53.808 --> 00:39:57.143
Thanks, Jack.
You truly are my dearest friend.


00:40:02.316 --> 00:40:05.402
Senator Jarvis, I have a check for
you from the Choctaw Indians.


00:40:05.486 --> 00:40:07.278
Oh.
Press my "easy button," Jack.


00:40:07.363 --> 00:40:09.280
And they want to wish you the
best with your campaign.


00:40:09.365 --> 00:40:11.658
I want to, uh, congratulate
and thank each of you...


00:40:11.742 --> 00:40:15.078
for getting involved in politics
through Young Republicans.


00:40:15.162 --> 00:40:17.914
What you're doing is commendable
and important because,


00:40:17.998 --> 00:40:21.292
as goes politics, so
goes our country.


00:40:21.377 --> 00:40:24.587
Grover. And a weak country
cannot provide the world...


00:40:24.672 --> 00:40:26.589
Glad you're on the team.


00:40:27.883 --> 00:40:31.553
Jack, you know how I
feel about freebies.


00:40:31.637 --> 00:40:35.557
Poncho is the third Indian you've
made me babysit this month.


00:40:35.641 --> 00:40:38.643
There is only so much congressmen
at Americans for Tax Reform...


00:40:38.727 --> 00:40:42.063
want to be educated about the
benefits of Indian gaming.


00:40:42.690 --> 00:40:44.232
Grover.


00:40:46.193 --> 00:40:49.279
Well, Grover, how about we fatten
Poncho's donation to A.T.R.,


00:40:49.363 --> 00:40:51.281
help you out with your
operational costs?


00:40:51.365 --> 00:40:55.118
That'd be a start.
I have a hole in my budget of 75K.


00:40:55.202 --> 00:40:57.370
Ouch. All right.
I'll look into it, champ.


00:40:57.455 --> 00:40:59.747
Meanwhile, where the
fuck is your evil elf?


00:40:59.832 --> 00:41:03.918
Mikey boy? He was supposed to take
Poncho off my hands three hours ago.


00:41:11.051 --> 00:41:14.137
You guys want to see
something crazy? Bam!


00:41:14.221 --> 00:41:17.015
A million smackeroos, baby.
Give me five.


00:41:17.099 --> 00:41:20.101
How sexy am I to you
right now, huh?


00:41:20.186 --> 00:41:21.811
Very sexy. Right?


00:41:21.896 --> 00:41:24.898
- Sure you're not a drug dealer or something, baby?
- Drug dealer, my ass.


00:41:24.982 --> 00:41:26.691
Oh. Your lackey's defending you.


00:41:26.775 --> 00:41:29.444
Jack and I are doing
God's work, baby.


00:41:29.528 --> 00:41:31.528
And you don't think the
Indian Affairs Committee...


00:41:31.572 --> 00:41:34.092
is gonna take issue with all the
high fees you've been charging?


00:41:34.116 --> 00:41:36.618
Since when have you become
an expert on Indian affairs?


00:41:36.702 --> 00:41:39.162
You're not the only one who knows a thing
or two about Washington, you know.


00:41:39.246 --> 00:41:42.749
Those bitches are doing the exact same
thing we are... trying to open casinos.


00:41:42.833 --> 00:41:44.751
They're just jealous...


00:41:44.835 --> 00:41:47.295
'cause they don't
make as much as you.


00:41:47.379 --> 00:41:49.088
You are so right.


00:41:55.679 --> 00:41:58.097
Here it is, baby.


00:41:58.182 --> 00:42:00.725
Shangri-la, Kubla Khan, Xanadu.


00:42:07.191 --> 00:42:09.442
Ooh. Hey. Sorry, babe.


00:42:10.819 --> 00:42:13.154
Ah? Oh, my God.


00:42:13.239 --> 00:42:16.658
What? You don't like?
This is high-end?


00:42:16.742 --> 00:42:18.660
This is like something you'd
find in Southampton, right?


00:42:18.744 --> 00:42:20.912
Southampton.
Have you ever been to Southampton?


00:42:20.996 --> 00:42:22.914
This is great for
Delaware, dude.


00:42:22.998 --> 00:42:25.375
Right? A little bit of
paint here and there.


00:42:25.459 --> 00:42:27.460
Come on.
Mike, have you lost your mind?


00:42:27.545 --> 00:42:29.963
It's a what?


00:42:30.047 --> 00:42:32.715
A Zamboni.


00:42:32.800 --> 00:42:36.052
A Zamboni machine for smoothing
out the surface of the ice.


00:42:36.136 --> 00:42:37.679
What ice?


00:42:37.763 --> 00:42:40.265
The ice for the hockey rink.
A hockey rink?


00:42:40.349 --> 00:42:42.392
I don't see a hockey rink.
Well, no. Not here.


00:42:42.476 --> 00:42:44.561
It's being built somewhere else.
Honey.


00:42:44.645 --> 00:42:46.604
Look. These are all
temporary facilities.


00:42:46.689 --> 00:42:50.066
It's all part of the new Eshkol
Academy and Sports Center...


00:42:50.150 --> 00:42:52.318
that I'm building for all
these kids... for our kids.


00:42:52.403 --> 00:42:54.320
You were serious about
building a school?


00:42:54.405 --> 00:42:57.782
Well, of course. You know how I feel about
the education that these kids are getting.


00:42:57.866 --> 00:42:59.367
A hockey rink?


00:42:59.451 --> 00:43:00.910
